{% comment %}
  A single guide page - the ring sizer, the wrist sizer, gemstones, jewellery care.

  The guides are ordinary Shopify pages: a title and a block of rich text, with a
  photo and, on the ring guide, an international conversion chart. The default page
  template rendered that at full browser width with no measure and no table styling,
  which is what made them hard to read.

  This gives the same content a hero that matches the Education & Guides hub, a
  readable column, and a row of sibling guides at the foot so a reader always has
  somewhere to go next. A card whose link points at the page being viewed drops out,
  so a guide never offers itself.

  Looks come from assets/editorial-cards.css, shared with the hub and the blog.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'editorial-cards.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'editorial-downloads.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- liquid
  assign stts = section.settings
  assign columns = stts.columns | default: 4

  assign columns_tablet = 2
  if columns < 2
    assign columns_tablet = columns
  endif

  assign heading = stts.heading | default: page.title

  comment
    Keep the page copy in Shopify's page editor, but let each guide block replace
    the first five body photos from the theme editor. Replacing the image URL path
    updates both src and srcset variants while preserving the editor's layout.
  endcomment
  assign guide_content = page.content
  assign sizer_download_image = blank
  for content_guide in section.blocks
    if content_guide.settings.link != page.url
      continue
    endif

    if page.handle == 'wrist-sizer-guide' and content_guide.settings.body_image_3 != blank
      assign sizer_download_image = content_guide.settings.body_image_3 | image_url
    endif

    for image_number in (1..5)
      assign body_image_setting = 'body_image_' | append: image_number
      assign body_image = content_guide.settings[body_image_setting]
      if body_image == blank
        continue
      endif

      assign content_images = guide_content | split: '<img'
      if content_images.size <= image_number
        continue
      endif

      assign content_image_attrs = content_images[image_number] | split: '>' | first
      assign content_image_src_parts = content_image_attrs | split: 'src="'
      if content_image_src_parts.size < 2
        continue
      endif

      assign content_image_src = content_image_src_parts[1] | split: '"' | first
      assign content_image_path = content_image_src | split: '?' | first
      assign body_image_url = body_image | image_url: width: 1600
      assign body_image_path = body_image_url | split: '?' | first
      assign guide_content = guide_content | replace: content_image_path, body_image_path
    endfor
    break
  endfor

  comment
    The banner hero. A guide's picture can come from the admin (image_picker) or
    from the theme's own files (image_asset), the same pair the cards below use,
    so a guide drawn from theme assets gets a banner too.
  endcomment
  assign section_hero_image = stts.hero_image
  assign section_hero_asset = stts.hero_image_asset | strip
  assign hero_image = blank
  assign hero_asset = blank

  comment
    This template serves several guides. Use the matching guide block's banner
    image so each page gets its own subject without duplicating the template.
    A dedicated banner image wins; the card image is the fallback.
  endcomment
  assign use_page_image = false
  for guide_block in section.blocks
    if guide_block.settings.link != page.url
      continue
    endif

    if guide_block.settings.hero_use_page_image
      assign use_page_image = true
      break
    endif

    assign hero_image = guide_block.settings.hero_image
    if hero_image == blank
      assign hero_asset = guide_block.settings.hero_image_asset | strip
    endif
    if hero_image == blank and hero_asset == blank
      assign hero_image = guide_block.settings.image
    endif
    if hero_image == blank and hero_asset == blank
      assign hero_asset = guide_block.settings.image_asset | strip
    endif
    break
  endfor

  comment
    Guide-specific choices take priority. Section-wide choices are a fallback
    for a page with no matching guide image configured on its block.
  endcomment
  if hero_image == blank and hero_asset == blank and use_page_image == false
    assign hero_image = section_hero_image
    if hero_image == blank
      assign hero_asset = section_hero_asset
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Nothing picked and nothing named in assets: borrow the page's own opening
    photograph. These guides were all written the same way - the picture first,
    the words beneath it - so the shot the editor already chose is the right one,
    and lifting it saves hand-setting a banner on every guide. It is cut from the
    body below (featured_src) so the reader is not shown it twice.
  endcomment
  assign hero_lift_src = ''
  assign hero_lift_alt = ''
  if hero_image == blank and hero_asset == blank and stts.hero_image_source == 'lift'
    assign img_tags = guide_content | split: '<img'
    if img_tags.size > 1
      assign first_attrs = img_tags[1] | split: '>' | first
      assign src_parts = first_attrs | split: 'src="'
      if src_parts.size > 1
        assign hero_lift_src = src_parts[1] | split: '"' | first
      endif
      assign alt_parts = first_attrs | split: 'alt="'
      if alt_parts.size > 1
        assign hero_lift_alt = alt_parts[1] | split: '"' | first
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    The CDN takes a width through the query string. Every file URL Shopify writes
    already carries "?v=", but one pasted in by hand may not.
  endcomment
  assign lift_join = '&'
  unless hero_lift_src contains '?'
    assign lift_join = '?'
  endunless

  assign has_hero_media = false
  if hero_image != blank or hero_asset != blank or hero_lift_src != blank
    assign has_hero_media = true
  endif

  comment
    Whichever of the three the header ended up with, the body is told to drop it.
  endcomment
  assign featured_src = hero_image.src | default: hero_lift_src

  assign banner_class = 'eg-banner eg-banner--' | append: stts.hero_width
  case stts.hero_align
    when 'left'
      assign banner_class = banner_class | append: ' eg-banner--left'
    when 'bottom'
      assign banner_class = banner_class | append: ' eg-banner--bottom'
    when 'bottom-left'
      assign banner_class = banner_class | append: ' eg-banner--bottom eg-banner--left'
  endcase
  unless has_hero_media
    assign banner_class = banner_class | append: ' eg-banner--plain'
  endunless

  comment
    Find the opening paragraph: the first "<p>...</p>" carrying actual words,
    looked for in the first few paragraph-sized chunks rather than only at
    character nought, because a page may open on a heading, a stray wrapper or
    a picture. Only the paragraph itself is lifted - whatever sits in front of
    it is left exactly where the editor put it.
  endcomment
  assign lead_html = ''
  assign lead_words = ''
  if stts.subheading == blank and stts.hero_text_source == 'lift'
    assign lead_chunks = guide_content | split: '</p>'
    for chunk in lead_chunks limit: 4
      assign chunk_parts = chunk | split: '<p'
      if chunk_parts.size < 2
        continue
      endif
      assign para_tail = chunk_parts | last
      assign para_html = '<p' | append: para_tail | append: '</p>'
      assign para_words = para_html | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: ' ', ' ' | strip
      if para_words != blank
        assign lead_html = para_html
        assign lead_words = para_words
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign media_sizes = '100vw'
  if stts.hero_style == 'split'
    assign media_sizes = '(min-width: 850px) 50vw, 100vw'
  endif

  assign split_class = 'eg-hero-split eg-hero-split--' | append: stts.hero_width
  if stts.hero_split_flip
    assign split_class = split_class | append: ' eg-hero-split--flipped'
  endif
  if stts.hero_split_mobile == 'picture'
    assign split_class = split_class | append: ' eg-hero-split--picture-first'
  endif
  unless has_hero_media
    assign split_class = split_class | append: ' eg-hero-split--solo'
  endunless

  assign scrim_alpha = stts.hero_overlay | divided_by: 100.0
  assign wash_alpha = stts.hero_wash | divided_by: 100.0
  assign pill_alpha = stts.hero_eyebrow_opacity | divided_by: 100.0
-%}

{%- style -%}
  #guide-page-{{ section.id }} {
    --eg-columns-desktop: {{ columns }};
    --eg-columns-tablet: {{ columns_tablet }};
    --eg-ink: {{ stts.text_color }};
    --eg-muted: {{ stts.muted_text_color }};
    --eg-card-bg: {{ stts.card_background }};
    --eg-card-border: {{ stts.card_border_color }};
    --eg-accent: {{ stts.accent_color }};
    --eg-radius: {{ stts.card_radius }}px;
    --eg-gap: {{ stts.card_gap | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-ratio: {{ stts.image_ratio }};
    --gp-more-align: {{ stts.more_heading_align }};
    --gp-text-col: {{ stts.split_text_width | default: 36 }}%;
    --eg-heading-size: {{ stts.heading_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-body-size: {{ stts.body_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-card-title-size: {{ stts.card_title_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-card-text-size: {{ stts.card_text_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-banner-height: {{ stts.hero_height | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-banner-height-mobile: {{ stts.hero_height_mobile | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-banner-radius: {{ stts.hero_radius }}px;
    --eg-banner-ink: {{ stts.hero_text_color }};
    --eg-banner-focus: {{ stts.hero_focal }};
    --eg-banner-scrim: {{ stts.hero_overlay_color | color_modify: 'alpha', scrim_alpha }};
    --eg-banner-wash: {{ stts.hero_overlay_color | color_modify: 'alpha', wash_alpha }};
    --eg-banner-fallback: {{ stts.hero_fallback_color }};
    --eg-banner-pill-bg: {{ stts.hero_eyebrow_background | color_modify: 'alpha', pill_alpha }};
    --eg-banner-pill-ink: {{ stts.hero_eyebrow_text_color }};
    --eg-banner-btn-bg: {{ stts.hero_button_background }};
    --eg-banner-btn-ink: {{ stts.hero_button_text_color }};
    --eg-split-text: {{ stts.hero_split_ratio }}%;
    --eg-split-bg: {{ stts.hero_split_background }};
    --eg-split-ink: {{ stts.hero_text_color }};
    --eg-split-media-height: {{ stts.hero_split_media_height | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-split-fit: {{ stts.hero_split_fit | default: 'cover' }};
    --eg-split-media-bg: {{ stts.hero_split_media_background | default: stts.hero_split_background }};
    --eg-banner-heading-size: {{ stts.hero_heading_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-banner-text-size: {{ stts.hero_text_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-cta-bg: {{ stts.cta_background }};
    --eg-cta-ink: {{ stts.cta_text_color }};
    --eg-btn-bg: {{ stts.cta_button_background }};
    --eg-btn-ink: {{ stts.cta_button_text_color }};
    background: {{ stts.background }};
    color: {{ stts.text_color }};
    padding-block: {{ stts.padding_top }}px {{ stts.padding_bottom }}px;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<section
  id="guide-page-{{ section.id }}"
  class="editorial-cards guide-page{% if page.handle == 'jewellery-care' %} guide-page--jewellery-care{% endif %} color-{{ stts.color_scheme }}"
>
  <div class="eg-shell">
    {%- comment -%}
      The eyebrow, title and line are the same words whichever shape the header
      takes, so they are written once here and placed by each shape below.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture hero_copy -%}
      {%- if stts.eyebrow != blank -%}
        {%- if stts.eyebrow_link != blank -%}
          <a class="eg-eyebrow" href="{{ stts.eyebrow_link }}">{{ stts.eyebrow | escape }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="eg-eyebrow">{{ stts.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        <h1 class="eg-heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if stts.subheading != blank -%}
        <div class="eg-banner__text rte">{{ stts.subheading }}</div>
      {%- elsif lead_words != blank -%}
        <p class="eg-banner__text">{{ lead_words }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if stts.hero_button_label != blank and stts.hero_button_link != blank -%}
        <a class="eg-banner__button eden-action eden-action--solid" href="{{ stts.hero_button_link }}">
          {{- stts.hero_button_label | escape -}}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- capture hero_media -%}
      {%- if hero_image != blank -%}
        {{
          hero_image
          | image_url: width: 2400
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'high',
            widths: '600, 900, 1200, 1600, 2000, 2400',
            sizes: media_sizes,
            alt: heading
        }}
      {%- elsif hero_asset != blank -%}
        <img
          src="{{ hero_asset | asset_img_url: '2400x' }}"
          srcset="
            {{ hero_asset | asset_img_url: '900x' }} 900w,
            {{ hero_asset | asset_img_url: '1600x' }} 1600w,
            {{ hero_asset | asset_img_url: '2400x' }} 2400w
          "
          sizes="{{ media_sizes }}"
          alt="{{ heading | escape }}"
          width="2400"
          height="1350"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          data-gp-hero-asset
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          src="{{ hero_lift_src }}{{ lift_join }}width=1600"
          srcset="
            {{ hero_lift_src }}{{ lift_join }}width=900 900w,
            {{ hero_lift_src }}{{ lift_join }}width=1600 1600w,
            {{ hero_lift_src }}{{ lift_join }}width=2400 2400w
          "
          sizes="{{ media_sizes }}"
          alt="{{ hero_lift_alt | default: heading | escape }}"
          width="1600"
          height="900"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        >
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- if stts.hero_style == 'split' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Words one side against a flat panel, the photograph whole on the other.
        These guides are shot on white, so a title laid over the picture has to
        fight it for contrast; here it does not have to.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="{{ split_class }}">
        <div class="eg-hero-split__copy">{{ hero_copy }}</div>

        {%- if has_hero_media -%}
          <div class="eg-hero-split__media">{{ hero_media }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- elsif stts.hero_style == 'banner' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The picture is the header: the guide's title sits in the middle of it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="{{ banner_class }}">
        {%- if has_hero_media -%}
          <div class="eg-banner__media">{{ hero_media }}</div>
          <span class="eg-banner__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="eg-banner__inner">{{ hero_copy }}</div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="gp-hero">{{ hero_copy }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div
      class="gp-content rte"
      {% if stts.force_downloads %}data-editorial-downloads{% endif %}
      {% if page.handle == 'er-sizing' %}data-sizer-download="finger"
      {% elsif page.handle == 'wrist-sizer-guide' %}data-sizer-download="wrist"{% endif %}
      {% if sizer_download_image != blank %}data-sizer-download-src="{{ sizer_download_image }}"{% endif %}
    >
      {%- render 'editorial-content',
        content: guide_content,
        split_sections: stts.split_sections,
        scroll_tables: stts.scroll_tables,
        featured_src: featured_src,
        lead_html: lead_html
      -%}
    </div>

    {%- if stts.show_more and section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      {%- liquid
        comment
          A card pointing at the page being read is dropped, so a guide never offers
          itself. Compared on the path alone, because a block's link is stored as a
          relative URL while page.url carries no query or anchor either.
        endcomment
        assign current_path = page.url
        assign more_count = 0
        for block in section.blocks
          if block.settings.title == blank
            continue
          endif
          if block.settings.link == current_path
            continue
          endif
          assign more_count = more_count | plus: 1
        endfor
      -%}

      {%- if more_count > 0 -%}
        <div class="gp-more">
          {%- if stts.more_heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="gp-more__heading">{{ stts.more_heading | escape }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}

          <ul class="eg-grid eg-grid--flat" role="list">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign title = block.settings.title
                if title == blank
                  continue
                endif
                if block.settings.link == current_path
                  continue
                endif

                assign picture = block.settings.image
                assign picture_asset = blank
                if picture == blank
                  assign picture_asset = block.settings.image_asset | strip
                endif

                assign shared_picture = blank
                case block.settings.link
                  when '/blogs/education-guides/4cs'
                    assign shared_picture = settings.guide_image_four_cs
                  when '/pages/gemstones'
                    assign shared_picture = settings.guide_image_gemstones
                  when '/pages/er-sizing'
                    assign shared_picture = settings.guide_image_ring_size
                  when '/pages/wrist-sizer-guide'
                    assign shared_picture = settings.guide_image_wrist_size
                  when '/pages/jewellery-care'
                    assign shared_picture = settings.guide_image_care
                endcase
                if shared_picture != blank
                  assign picture = shared_picture
                  assign picture_asset = blank
                endif

                assign has_media = false
                if stts.show_images
                  if picture != blank or picture_asset != blank
                    assign has_media = true
                  endif
                endif

                assign has_link = false
                if block.settings.link != blank
                  assign has_link = true
                endif
              -%}

              <li class="eg-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {%- if has_link -%}
                  <a class="eg-card__link eden-action-host" href="{{ block.settings.link }}">
                {%- else -%}
                  <div class="eg-card__link">
                {%- endif -%}

                  {%- if has_media -%}
                    <div class="eg-card__media">
                      {%- if picture != blank -%}
                        {{
                          picture
                          | image_url: width: 900
                          | image_tag:
                            loading: 'lazy',
                            sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 33vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw',
                            alt: title
                        }}
                      {%- else -%}
                        <img
                          src="{{ picture_asset | asset_img_url: '900x' }}"
                          srcset="
                            {{ picture_asset | asset_img_url: '450x' }} 450w,
                            {{ picture_asset | asset_img_url: '900x' }} 900w
                          "
                          sizes="(min-width: 990px) 33vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw"
                          alt="{{ title | escape }}"
                          width="900"
                          height="900"
                          loading="lazy"
                          data-gp-asset
                        >
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}

                  <div class="eg-card__body">
                    <h3 class="eg-card__title">{{ title | escape }}</h3>

                    {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
                      <p class="eg-card__text">{{ block.settings.text | escape }}</p>
                    {%- endif -%}

                    {%- if has_link -%}
                      <span class="eg-card__cta eden-link">
                        {{- block.settings.link_label | default: 'Read the guide' | escape -}}
                        <span class="eg-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>

                {%- if has_link -%}
                  </a>
                {%- else -%}
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if stts.show_cta and stts.cta_heading != blank -%}
      <div class="eg-cta">
        <div class="eg-cta__copy">
          <p class="eg-cta__heading">{{ stts.cta_heading | escape }}</p>
          {%- if stts.cta_text != blank -%}
            <div class="eg-cta__text rte">{{ stts.cta_text }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if stts.cta_button_label != blank and stts.cta_button_link != blank -%}
          <a class="eg-cta__button eden-action eden-action--outline" href="{{ stts.cta_button_link }}">
            {{- stts.cta_button_label | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  A card can name a file under assets/ the shop has not uploaded. Rather than leave a
  broken frame the picture is dropped and the card carries on as type.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (() => {
    const root = document.getElementById('guide-page-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root) return;
    root.querySelectorAll('img[data-gp-asset], img[data-gp-hero-asset]').forEach((img) => {
      img.addEventListener('error', () => {
        const media = img.closest('.eg-card__media, .eg-banner__media');
        media?.remove();
        if (img.hasAttribute('data-gp-hero-asset')) {
          root.querySelector('.eg-banner')?.classList.add('eg-banner--plain');
        }
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Guide page",
  "class": "section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Hero"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "hero_style",
      "label": "Header style",
      "options": [
        { "value": "split", "label": "Split - words one side, photo the other" },
        { "value": "banner", "label": "Banner - title over the photo" },
        { "value": "stacked", "label": "Stacked - title on the page background" }
      ],
      "default": "split",
      "info": "The banner puts the guide's title in the middle of a full photo, with one line of copy beneath it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "Education & guides"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "eyebrow_link",
      "label": "Eyebrow link",
      "info": "Usually the guides hub, so a reader can get back to the list."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the page's own title."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Standfirst"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Banner" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "hero_text_source",
      "label": "When no subheading is typed",
      "options": [
        { "value": "lift", "label": "Move the opening paragraph onto the photo" },
        { "value": "none", "label": "Show nothing under the title" }
      ],
      "default": "lift",
      "info": "Moving it takes the paragraph out of the body as well, so it is not read twice."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "hero_image_source",
      "label": "When no photo is set below",
      "options": [
        { "value": "lift", "label": "Use the page's own first picture" },
        { "value": "none", "label": "Show no photo" }
      ],
      "default": "lift",
      "info": "Taking it moves the picture out of the body as well, so it is not seen twice."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "hero_image",
      "label": "Banner photo"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_image_asset",
      "label": "Banner photo from the theme files",
      "info": "A file name in assets, e.g. guide-rings.jpg. Used only when no photo is picked above."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hero_button_label", "label": "Button label", "info": "Leave empty for no button." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "hero_button_link", "label": "Button link" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Split header" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "hero_split_ratio",
      "label": "The words' share",
